      "description": "Job Opportunities | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Adjunct Faculty, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Adjunct Faculty, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Shawnee State University (OH) Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Adjunct Faculty, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts Print Apply ﻿ Adjunct Faculty, Fine, Digital & Performing Arts Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-034 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-CAS-Fine, Digital & Performing Arts Opening Date 04/20/2026 Closing Date 1/10/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary Job Description Summary The Department of Fine, Digital, and Performing Arts invites applications for all semesters for part-time adjunct teaching positions. These are semester-to-semester positions primarily teaching introductory sections of the following areas, both in person and online. Acting Art History Audio Design Ceramics Dance Digital 3D Drawing Figure Drawing Game Development Arts Graphic Arts Musical Theatre Painting Photography Piano lessons The Department of Fine, Digital, and Performing Arts at Shawnee State is an incubator for creativity. Majors, Minors, and GEP courses in the arts enable students to cultivate and expand their skills across several arts disciplines. The department faculty value technical skill, aesthetic dialogue, professionalism, open individual expression, and reasoned critique. Applications are accepted continuously. All applicants must complete the online application at Shawnee.edu . Upload a cover letter to Human Resources specifically addressing how your qualifications meet the posted qualifications Your resume/curriculum vitae (including a link to a portfolio of relevant work), and An unofficial transcript indicating the highest degree attained. IMPORTANT NOTE ABOUT REFERENCE SECTION : Include the name, email address, and phone number of your Professional References. Candidates invited for an on-campus interview may be required to deliver a teaching lecture and a laboratory demonstration to demonstrate their instructional abilities. Specific questions may be directed to Dr. Greg Lyons, Chair of the Department of Fine, Digital, and Performing Arts at 740.351.3004. Adjunct faculty at SSU are also eligible for tuition waivers ( Tuition Waiver for Adjunct Faculty Policy (Download PDF reader) ) and enjoy professional development opportunities, office space, and limited mileage reimbursement. They and their family (children 14 years and up) also have free access to the Rhodes Athletic Facility. Employment with the University is dependent upon BOT budget approval for the current fiscal year. A background check is required prior to hire. Official transcripts are required and must be submitted prior to hire to Dr. Michael Barnhart, Interim Dean of the College of Arts & Sciences at 940 2nd Street, Portsmouth, OH 45662. Note to Applicants - This is an open posting maintained and updated every semester based upon the enrollment needs of the Department and, as such, is filled on an as-needed/ongoing basis every semester. SSU seeks individuals who share our commitment to students as our first priority. Shawnee State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against any individual because of race, color, genetic information, religion, age, disability, national origin, ancestry, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, veteran status or military status. Minimum Qualifications MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS (EDUCATION, KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, ABILITIES, AND EXPERIENCE) Master’s Degree in the subject or closely related area A willingness to engage students thoughtfully and critically in the subject area Ability to communicate clearly to students Basic knowledge of instructional software and ability to teach online courses Ability to work closely and effectively with diverse populations in all aspects PREFERRED QUALIFICATION Knowledge of different pedagogical strategies Prior teaching experience both in person and online MFA or PhD in the area being taught or closely related area This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job 