    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/ssuoh/jobs/5440423/assistant-professor-of-psychology-biopsychology-social-and-or-developmental-neur": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Psychology (Biopsychology/Social and/or Developmental Neuroscience)",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Assistant Professor of Psychology (Biopsychology/Social and/or Developmental Neuroscience) | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Assistant Professor of Psychology (Biopsychology/Social and/or Developmental Neuroscience) | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Shawnee State University (OH) Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Assistant Professor of Psychology (Biopsychology/Social and/or Developmental Neuroscience) Print Apply ﻿ Assistant Professor of Psychology (Biopsychology/Social and/or Developmental Neuroscience) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Full-Time Job Number POS-873 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-CAS-Social Sciences Opening Date 08/20/2026 Description Benefits Job Description Summary The Department of Psychology at Shawnee State Universit y (SSU) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Psychology . We seek a psychologist with expertise in either Biopsychology, Physiological Psychology, Behavioral Neuroscience, Cognitive Neuroscience, or a closely related field . The anticipated start date is either January 2027 or August 2027 Shawnee State University is a student-centered public university located in Portsmouth, Ohio, a small community along the Ohio River. We serve a student population that includes many first-generation college students. At SSU, faculty can make a meaningful difference through excellent teaching, mentorship, and campus/community engagement. We seek a colleague who is committed to undergraduate education, excited to work with students, and able to teach effectively in both face-to-face and online formats. The successful candidate will be willing to contribute to the campus community. Areas of Expertise Primary expertise should be in Biopsychology / Physiological Psychology or a closely related area. Related fields may include: Behavioral Neuroscience / Biological Psychology Cognitive Neuroscience / Affective Neuroscience Experimental Psychology with a neuroscience or brain-behavior emphasis Sensation and Perception Learning and Memory with a neuroscience emphasis Neuropsychology with a non-clinical or experimental emphasis Comparative, evolutionary, or biological approaches to brain and behavior Responsibilities The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, advising, scholarship, curriculum development, and service. Teaching The position requires a 4/4 undergraduate course load, with four courses each fall and spring semester. The department values candidates who can teach broadly across the psychology curriculum. Priority teaching areas include: PSYC 3150 Neurobiology of Behavior PSYC 3151 Sensation and Perception PSYC 3152 Cognitive Neuroscience PSYC 4150 Physiology of Behavior (course with lab) PSYC 4151 Evolutionary Psychology The ability to teach core courses such as statistics, research methods or other departmental needs is also valued. Curriculum Development Help maintain and strengthen the department’s offerings in biopsychology, neuroscience, and related areas . Contribute to a reliable rotation of upper-division courses that supports student progress toward graduation. Student Mentorship and Advising Advise and mentor undergraduate students, including first-generation students and students from diverse educational backgrounds. Support students as they develop career plans, research interests, and professional skills. Scholarly Engagement Engage in research, applied scholarship, or professional activity appropriate to the discipline and institutional mission. Student involvement in scholarly work is highly encouraged. Service and Campus Engagement Participate in department, college, and university service. The department values candidates who are willing to be present, active, collegial members of the campus community. Application Process The search committee will begin reviewing applications after the job has been posted for at least 3 weeks and will continue until the position is filled. To apply, please submit the following materials through the university’s online application system: 1. Cover Letter Addressed to Dean, College of Arts & Sciences. The letter should describe how your qualifications, teaching interests/experiences, and professional goals fit the position, with particular attention to your commitment to undergraduate instruction and the campus community. 2. Curriculum Vitae Current and comprehensive. 3. Teaching Philosophy Statement A 1–2 page statement describing your approach to teaching, student engagement, and mentoring. 4. Unofficial Transcripts Graduate coursework representing the highest degree attained. Official transcripts will be required upon hire. 5. References Contact information for three professional references who can speak to your qualifications. Candidates invited for an interview will be required to present a teaching sample, such as a lecture, to demonstrate instructional effectiveness. Specific questions about the position may be directed to: Dr. Rhoni Maxwell-Rader, Psychology Program Coordinator, at Rmaxwellrader@shawnee.edu. Shawnee State University is the regional state university for South-Central Ohio. It is a primarily undergraduate, four-year public university with limited graduate degree programs. Enrollment is approximately 3,500 students. Shawnee State is located on the Ohio River in Portsmouth, Ohio – a small city nestled in a beautiful, rural area of Southern Ohio. Portsmouth is approximately an hour drive from Huntington, WV, and two hours from Columbus or Cincinnati, Ohio. Additional information about SSU is available at www.shawnee.edu . Shawnee State offers a competitive salary (commensurate with experience and qualifications) including an attractive benefits package (see Overview of Employee Benefits for more information). Employment with the University is dependent upon BOT budget approval for the fiscal year. Official transcripts and a background check are required prior to hire. SSU seeks individuals who share our commitment to students as our first priority. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment. Our institution prepares students to engage with diverse people, perspectives, and communities. We value the differences, similarities, and unique contributions of individuals. We strive to model diversity and inclusion in our campus community. Shawnee State University is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity Employer. The University prohibits discrimination against any individual because of race, color, genetic information, religion, age, disability, national origin, ancestry, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status or military status. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must meet one of the following qualifications: (Preferred) A doctorate, Ph.D. or equivalent, in Biopsychology, Physiological Psychology, Behavioral Neuroscience, Cognitive Neuroscience, Experimental Psychology, or a closely related field by the start date; or ABD status in one of the listed or closely related fields, with a documented pathway to degree completion within one year of hire; or A master’s degree in a listed or closely related field with at least three years of full-time college-level teaching experience or five years of relevant professional experience in a neuroscience, biopsychology, or brain-behavior related role. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS College-level teaching experience. Strong commitment to undergraduate teaching, advising, and mentorship. Ability to teach a variety of psychology courses, including courses outside the candidate’s primary specialization. Ability to teach effectively in both face-to-face and online formats. Effective use of current instructional technology to engage students and support learning Interest in supporting first-generation college students and students from diverse backgrounds. Commitment to active participation in the department, campus, and/or local community. Interest in involving undergraduate students in research, applied projects, or scholarly activity. Ability to engage students, both attracting and retaining students within the psychology program. Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information.  Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                   