      "description": "Job Opportunities | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers Opens in a new window Opens an external website Opens an external website in a new window This website utilizes technologies such as cookies to enable essential site functionality, as well as for analytics, personalization, and targeted advertising. Privacy Policy Accept Deny Non-Essential Manage Preferences Close Cookie Preferences For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Operations Manager, Adena | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Operations Manager, Adena | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Skip to main content Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Saving... Account could not be created. Please fix the errors to continue. Sign In All fields are required Create an account Username or Email Password Sign In Forgot username | Reset password Sign in with Google Sign in with Google. Opens in new tab Facebook Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Shawnee State University (OH) Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Operations Manager, Adena Print Apply ﻿ Operations Manager, Adena Salary $54,440.00 - $61,245.00 Annually Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Full-Time Job Number POS-966 Division Academic and Student Affairs Department ASA-College of Health & Human Services Opening Date 08/10/2026 Closing Date 10/4/2026 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary The Additional Location Operations Manager serves as the primary institutional representative at Shawnee State’s additional location in Chillicothe, Ohio. They direct and manage the additional location operations at Chillicothe, providing oversight and direction for the operations of all degree and course offerings at this site. The position oversees and directs all processes related to the delivery of SSU programs and courses at the additional location, including: recruitment and enrollment processes for prospective students seeking programs/courses at this location, student and faculty support for enrolled students, and serving as the primary point of contact addressing all operational needs for SSU students, faculty/staff and Adena team members at SSU’s additional location (Chillicothe). Due to the location on the campus of the Adena Regional Medical Center and the primary health care focus of programs, healthcare leadership experience is required. Principal Duties and Responsibilities FUNCTIONS: Strategic Leadership and Operations Management for SSU Additional Location Partnership Development, Student Success. And Community Engagement Assessment, Data Analysis, and Continuous Improvement DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Strategic Leadership and Operations Management for SSU Additional Location Provides strategic leadership, operational oversight, and administrative management for all academic and student support functions at the site. Ensures effective delivery of academic programs, compliance with institutional and accreditation requirements, stakeholder satisfaction, and continuous operational improvement. Directs and manages all operational activities associated with the delivery of academic programs, courses, student services technology resources, facilities coordination, and institutional partnerships at the University’s additional location. Includes being point-of-contact for vendors engaged in service agreements for technology installed at additional location. Exercises independent judgement and decision-making authority regarding day-to-day operations, resource allocation, issue resolution, and stakeholder concerns to ensure uninterrupted delivery of academic programming and student support services. Key internal stakeholders include SSU administrative leadership, faculty, staff and external stakeholders include Adena administration and team members and community partners. Serves as University’s designated on-site administrator and institutional representative, ensuring alignment between University objectives and additional location operations. Coordinates cross-functional operational activities among Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, Student Affairs, Informational Technology Services, Facilities, Finance and external partners. Partnership Development, Student Success. And Community Engagement Develops and maintains strategic relationships that support enrollment growth, student success, academic quality, community partnerships, and institutional visibility at the additional location. Serves as primary University representative and relationship manager for all internal and external stakeholders associated with the additional location Develops, coordinates, and implements communication strategies that support enrollment, retention, stakeholder engagement, and effective operations. Implements recruitment and enrollment strategies and processes for SSU programs and courses at additional location in collaboration with CHHS Dean, relevant admissions team members (Director of Admissions, Chief Enrollment Officer, Admissions Associates, Advisors, Financial Aid, Student Accounts, Registrar, key faculty/program directors, etc). Plans, coordinates, and participates in student engagement and recruitment activities at various venues. Cultivates strategic partnerships with healthcare systems, community organizations, workforce partners, educational institutions, and regional employers to enhance program visibility and support enrollment growth. Serves as liaison and resource between all stakeholders, provides support and mentorship for new program/course implementation; ensures student support services are provided and facilitates student engagement at additional location. Other duties as assigned. Identifies barriers affecting student persistence and success and collaborates with university partners to implement solutions and interventions. Assessment, Data Analysis, and Continuous Improvement Uses data-informed decision-making processes to evaluate operational effectiveness, student outcomes, stakeholder satisfaction, enrollment trends and program success at the additional location. Develops, implements, and monitors performance metrics and assessment processes to evaluate operational effectiveness and support institution/program reporting requirements. Ensures alignment with university policies and procedures, and supports compliance with HLC requirements for additional location. Analyzes operational, enrollment, retention, and student success data; recommends and implements improvements that enhance service quality, efficiency, and student outcomes Prepares reports, recommendations, and strategic planning information for University leadership regarding additional location performance and future growth opportunities Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Ability to work collaboratively within SSU systems and with external stakeholders to provide leadership for the implementation of additional location program/course offerings. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills Ability to independently manage multiple tasks, prioritize effectively, and work in a fast-paced environment Excellent organizational and problem-solving skills, as well as attention to detail Minimum Qualifications Minimum required: Bachelors in Health Care Administration, Business Administration, Higher Ed Administration, Organizational Leadership or related field. Degrees in health discipline also acceptable. Must have 5 years of progressively responsible professional experience and 3 years of leadership, supervisory, project management, or operational management experience. Healthcare leadership experience is required. University driving approval Preferred: Masters degree in Healthcare Administration, Business Administration, Public Administration, Higher Education Administration, or Organizational Leadership. Experience in higher education. Experience in healthcare administration, Experience managing external and multiple stakeholder partnerships. Experience supporting academic program implementation. Directly relevant clinical and/or leadership experience in health field, preferably 5+ years in leadership role Strong understanding of and demonstrated ability to lead implementation of new initiatives Higher education work experience If health care provider, current licensure/credential preferred but not required. Working Conditions: This position is based in Chillicothe, with travel as needed to Portsmouth and outreach locations, occasional evening/weekend work for outreach. Normal office environment with little exposure to excessive dust, noise, heat and the like. Some lifting (up to 30 lbs.), walking, and driving required. Valid driver’s license with less than 3 moving violations. Travel and work evenings and/or weekends as needed for recruitment and outreach events. Work schedule adjusted accordingly. Shawnee State University offers a competitive starting salary (commensurate with overall qualifications) including an attractive benefits package. See Overview of Employee Benefits for more information.  Some of our benefits include: Paid Holidays Paid Winter Break in December Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Tuition Waiver Life Insurance Retirement Plans Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we a