      "title": "Part-time Assistant Coach, Athletic Teams",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Part-time Assistant Coach, Athletic Teams | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Part-time Assistant Coach, Athletic Teams | Shawnee State University (OH) Careers page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Shawnee State University (OH) Careers powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Part-time Assistant Coach, Athletic Teams Print Apply ﻿ Part-time Assistant Coach, Athletic Teams Salary Depends on Qualifications Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-Assist Coach Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Athletic/Intramurals Opening Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date 4/30/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary Part-time coaches within Shawnee State University Athletics—including both Head Coaches and Assistant Coaches—are responsible for supporting the planning, development, and administration of their respective athletic programs. These positions play an essential role in fostering a competitive, educational, and student-centered environment. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Tasks and Duties Performed Part-time coaches may be responsible for duties including, but not limited to: Coaching & Instruction Assist with planning and conducting practices, training sessions, and skill development. Provide instruction that aligns with program objectives, competitive standards, and student-athlete development. Support the development of game strategies and assist with in-game coaching. Program Administration Assist with roster management, communication with student-athletes, and maintaining practice and competition schedules. Support administrative tasks such as paperwork, equipment inventory, and program organization. Recruitment & Student-Athlete Support Assist in identifying and recruiting prospective student-athletes in accordance with university, conference, and NCAA guidelines (as applicable during transition periods). Promote academic success, personal development, and compliance among student-athletes. Event & Game-Day Operations Assist with game-day preparation, travel logistics, facility setup, and supervision of team activities. Represent the program and university in a professional manner at all athletic events. Compliance & Conduct Maintain knowledge of and adhere to all Shawnee State University, conference, and governing body rules and regulations. Report any known or suspected violations immediately to the Athletics Director or Compliance Office. Minimum Job Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Terms of Employment Hours will vary depending on sport, season, and departmental needs. All part-time employees must maintain an accurate record of hours worked and submit a completed timesheet at the end of each semester. Part-time coaches cannot work more than 125 hours per month, or 1500 hours over the appointment year, to ensure compliance with the Affordable Care Act. Continued employment is contingent upon adherence to all university and department policies, satisfactory performance, and program needs. Minimum Qualifications Required trainings: Concussion in Sports – yearly (online) (certification required) Concussion in Sports Course Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR), First Aid, and Automated External Defibrillator (AED) Training – every two years (Athletic Training/Red Cross) (certification required) Chapter 1 CPR Introduction - American CPR Care Association Sudden Cardiac Arrest – yearly (online) (certification required) NFHS Learn | Interscholastic Education, Made Easy Prior coaching or playing experience at the high school, collegiate, or professional level preferred. Strong communication, leadership, and organizational skills. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings, weekends, and travel as needed. Commitment to supporting student-athlete success academically, athletically, and personally. Ability to positively represent Shawnee State University and uphold the mission and values of the Athletics Department. Compliance With Policies All part-time athletic employees must comply with Shawnee State University policies and procedures as well as Shawnee State Athletics protocols. Failure to comply may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click