yee, Athletics, Game Day and Events - 26-27 Academic Year Salary $11.00 Hourly Location 940 Second St. Portsmouth, OH 45662, OH Job Type Part-Time Job Number POS-316 Division Advancement and Enrollment Management Department AEM-Athletic/Intramurals Opening Date 06/26/2026 Closing Date 5/9/2027 11:59 PM Eastern Description Benefits Job Description Summary ABOUT THE DEPARTMENT: For jobs that are included under the game operations, tasks that are involved with the athletic events that happen on and off campus. Those events will include: Soccer(M&W), Volleyball, Basketball (M&W), Swimming (M&W), Softball, and Baseball. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: The tasks that will be completed will be done at the highest level possible. You will be asked to complete tasks that potentially deals with fans, filming of an event, counting money, etc. Most of the tasks will be sport-specific, but there are some jobs that will be the same no matter the sport that is taking place. Those tasks are listed below: Taking Tickets Scoreboard Spotter/Music Film Stat Board/Stats Concessions Raffles Timers Managers ADDITIONAL INFORMATION: • Stats person(s), Tickets, Scoreboard - will only be handled once trust is built between you and your supervisor. • Heavy Lifting (50lbs or less) may be required • Availability to work late nights and weekends Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibili