along with focused study in polymer materials and properties, part and mold design, statistics, and computer-aided design. POSITION SUMMARY, ROUTINE TASKS & RESPONSIBILITIES: •  Acquire, maintain, and operate infrastructures, facilities, and equipment •  Provide an environment in which student outcomes can be attained • Maintaining appearance/cleanliness of labs • Maintain technical documentation for ABET Accreditation (both Reading & Writing) •  Assist in labs with faculty during scheduled classroom / lab times • Adhere to all safety standards and work practices established by the industry •  Assist other students with equipment and student projects •  Public speaking giving hands on presentations and demonstrations to industry & group tours •  Attend off campus recruiting events • Perform other duties as assigned • Participate in industry-partner laboratory projects, including injection molding trials and material property analysis. • Heavy Lifting (50 pounds) • Attained Sophomore status in the program • Registered full time in the Plastics Engineering Technology and or CAD Program • Technical Documentation (both Reading and Writing technical manuals) • Industrial Lab Equipment (Injection Molding, Extrusion, 3D printing, Materials Testing, Machining, etc.) • Industrial Safety • Demonstrated ability to direction and work with limited supervision Minimum Qualifications Registered full-time SSU student Eligible to work in the United States Strong communication and interpersonal skills Demonstrate reliability, punctuality, and follow instructions Ability to work independently and as part of a team Basic proficiency with Microsoft Office and social media platforms Follow SSU dress code policy This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Shawnee State University (OH) Address 940 Second St. Portsmouth, Ohio, 45662 Phone 740-351-3481 Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Pr